---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Jayson Petersen — what I work on, how I build, and where to find me."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I&rsquo;m Jayson Petersen. I build AI agents and the infrastructure they run on: schedulers
      that fetch and summarise, inference layers that spread load across whatever GPUs you have, and
      assistants that plug into real tools rather than a chat box.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of what I release is self-hosted and model-agnostic by design. If a project needs an LLM,
      it should work with the one you already run &mdash; local or hosted &mdash; and it should keep
      working when you swap it.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/jaypetez">github.com/jaypetez</a></li>
      <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> for the writing</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      Built with Astro, no client-side framework, and roughly 1.5&nbsp;KB of JavaScript on the wire
      &mdash; a theme toggle and link prefetching, nothing more. The <a
        href="https://github.com/jaypetez/jaypetez.github.io">source is public</a
      >, including the tests that keep the design honest.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
</style>
